  "name": "COMPLEMENT 3 (C3)",
  "code": "2001",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>C3 compoment is the central point of classic and alternative cdompliment pathway. Compliment testing helps to diagnose&nbsp;the cause of recurrent microbial infections, angioedema, inflamation and in acute or chronic autoimmune disease such as&nbsp;Systemic Lupus Erythematosus(SLE). Decreased levels of C3 are significant in autoimmune disease, recurrent infrections&nbsp;with pyrogenic bacteria, neonatal RDS and congential deficiencies. C3 behaves as an acute phase protein hence increased&nbsp;levels may found in acute inflammatory reactions. The reagent is linear up to 300mg/dl. Lower detection limit is 10mg/dl.</p>",
